<title>USA: Pep Boys Q4 Feb 1 net rises to $0.36/shr.</title>
<headline>Pep Boys Q4 Feb 1 net rises to $0.36/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.36		    $0.31</p>
<p> Net			 22,696		   18,620</p>
<p> Revs		     444,433		  410,506</p>
<p>		 YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.62		    $1.34</p>
<p> Net			100,824		   81,494</p>
<p> Revs		   1,828,539		1,594,340</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company's full name is Pep Boys -- Manny, Moe &amp; Jack.</p>
<p>First Call's Q4 consensus of analysts' estimates: $0.35 a share.</p>
<p>Period ended Feb 1 vs Feb 3.</p>
<p>Quarter is 13 weeks in 1997 vs 14 weeks in 1996.</p>
</text>
